.TH SPT 1  "spt 0.26.4" 
.SH NAME
spt \- Permanent SSH2/SSH3 tunnels with reconnect, observability, and service integration.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBspt\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-fingerprint\fR] [\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Permanent SSH2/SSH3 tunnels with reconnect, observability, and service integration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to a single config file
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Path to a directory of `*.toml` configs (loaded in lexical order)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
HTTPS URL of a remote config to fetch
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-fingerprint\fR \fI<SHA256>\fR
SHA\-256 fingerprint pin for `\-\-config\-url`
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Override the runtime state directory
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Restrict operations to the named profile
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: human]
Output format for command results
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Structured JSON
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: JSON Lines (one record per line)
.IP \(bu 2
yaml: YAML
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Convenience alias for `\-\-output json`
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR [default: info]
Tracing log level
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
error: Only errors
.IP \(bu 2
warn: Warnings and above
.IP \(bu 2
info: Informational and above (default)
.IP \(bu 2
debug: Debug and above
.IP \(bu 2
trace: Trace and above (very verbose)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
Color policy for human output
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Auto\-detect based on tty
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always emit color escapes
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never emit color escapes
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable color (legacy convenience flag; use `\-\-color never`)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would happen without making changes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
spt\-config(1)
Manage configuration files (init, validate, diff, render, reload)
.TP
spt\-profile(1)
Manage SSH/SSH3 tunnel profiles
.TP
spt\-forward(1)
Manage forwards (local/remote TCP, UDP)
.TP
spt\-tunnel(1)
Run, inspect, and control tunnels
.TP
spt\-service(1)
Install and control native services
.TP
spt\-key(1)
Generate, inspect, and install SSH keys
.TP
spt\-secret(1)
Manage the secret vault and OS keychain references
.TP
spt\-auth(1)
Authentication helpers
.TP
spt\-dns(1)
Built\-in DNS resolver and hosts\-file management
.TP
spt\-firewall(1)
Inspect and manage OS firewall / packet\-filter rules
.TP
spt\-log(1)
Log tailing, sink testing, and export
.TP
spt\-observe(1)
Metrics and Windows Event Log helpers
.TP
spt\-event(1)
Event bindings and sinks
.TP
spt\-stats(1)
Statistics summaries and live counters
.TP
spt\-session(1)
Inspect and manage active sessions
.TP
spt\-ftp(1)
FTP→SFTP translator service
.TP
spt\-sftp(1)
SFTP file operations and mount planning
.TP
spt\-diagnose(1)
Targeted diagnostics and support bundles
.TP
spt\-benchmark(1)
Controlled benchmarking against forwards
.TP
spt\-mcp(1)
Built\-in MCP server controls
.TP
spt\-status(1)
Read\-only status API controls (plan §t4\-e5)
.TP
spt\-completion(1)
Generate shell completions
.TP
spt\-about(1)
List bundled libraries and their licenses
.TP
spt\-kill(1)
Kill every running `spt` process on this host (cross\-platform)
.TP
spt\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.26.4
